{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group A of the 1978 FIFA World Cup''' was one of two groups of nations competing for the [[De facto]] semi-finals  the [[1978 FIFA World Cup]]. The group's first round of matches began on 14 June and its last matches were played on 21 June. All six group matches were played either at the [[Estadio Olímpico Chateau Carreras|Estadio Chateau Carreras]] in [[Córdoba, Argentina|Córdoba]], or the [[Estadio Monumental Antonio Vespucio Liberti|Estadio Monumental]] in the capital [[Buenos Aires]]. The group consisted of [[Germany national football team|West Germany]] (the Defending Champions) as well as the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]] (the former runners up), [[Italy national football team|Italy]] and [[Austria national football team|Austria]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/78full.html |title=World Cup 1978 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> The Netherlands advanced to the [[1978 FIFA World Cup final|final match]], and Italy advanced to the match for third place.<ref>{{cite web|title=World Cup Guide - 1978 Argentina|url=http://www.worldcupbrazil.net/world-cup-history/world-cup-70s-90s/1978-argentina/|work=worldcupbrazil.net|accessdate=5 July 2014|archive-date=1 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160301152208/http://www.worldcupbrazil.net/world-cup-history/world-cup-70s-90s/1978-argentina/|url-status=dead}}</ref>

