==Matches==

===Austria vs Netherlands===
After an unconvincing group stage performance the Netherlands knew they had to play better if they were to qualify for the finals, and took on surprise qualifiers Austria in their first game. They started well when an unmarked [[Ernie Brandts]] headed in [[Arie Haan]]'s free kick. The Dutch then won a penalty kick after [[Gerhard Breitenberger (footballer, born 1954)|Gerhard Breitenberger]] fouled [[Wim Jansen]] and [[Rob Rensenbrink]] neatly scored. Rensenbrink then took advantage of some poor defending to provide assist for [[Johnny Rep]] to score on either side of half time. Austria which created several chances and were unlucky to score in the first half got one back in the eightieth minute when defender [[Erich Obermayer]] scored a brilliant lob over the Dutch goalkeeper for a goal. The Dutch weren't to be deterred as Rensenbrink provided yet another assist this time [[Willy van de Kerkhof]] to score just two minutes later.<ref>{{cite web|title=Austria - Netherlands Match Report |url=http://www.planetworldcup.com/CUPS/1978/ph2gr1_hol_v_aut.html|work=Planet World Cup|accessdate=6 July 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=World Cup History: Argentina 1978|url=http://www.sportal.com.au/football/world-cup-2014/world-cup-history-argentina-1978/8ryb0kgibwe0zzhi3z2urkxb|work=Sportal|accessdate=6 July 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140714225832/http://www.sportal.com.au/football/world-cup-2014/world-cup-history-argentina-1978/8ryb0kgibwe0zzhi3z2urkxb|archive-date=14 July 2014|url-status=dead|df=dmy-all}}</ref>

